From 8196334f363d3c0f3e3acaa41f89cc9b954a022f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:16:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: prefetch the buffer of each completion of a chunk

The completion handler reads a chunk of up to 16 completions, then
releases their ids under one hold of the id lock. Each release reads the
id's table entry and, for a segment, the payload map of its extension
descriptor, both cold by then: in a profile of bridged downlink at
900 Mbit/s (IPQ8074, one run) the instruction after the table load in
ath11k_dp_tx_buf_put_id() takes 0.63 % of all samples and the one after
the map load 1.05 %. The id gives both addresses without another load, so
prefetch them for writing as each completion of the chunk is read; the
release then finds them arriving, 16 misses overlapped instead of taken
one after the other.

The prefetch of the frames two ahead covered the first two lines of the
sk_buff, while the prefetch of the shared info one ahead reads its address
from the third and fourth (end at offset 188, head at 192 on arm64): the
load after it takes 0.37 % of all samples. Prefetch those two lines with
the first two.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -1652,6 +1652,15 @@ int ath11k_dp_tx_completion_handler(stru
 					    it->tx_status->buf_addr_info.info1);
 			it->mac_id = FIELD_GET(DP_TX_DESC_ID_MAC_ID, desc_id);
 			it->msdu_id = FIELD_GET(DP_TX_DESC_ID_MSDU_ID, desc_id);
+			/* The id alone gives the addresses of its table entry
+			 * and payload map, which the release below writes:
+			 * start their loads for the whole chunk at once.
+			 */
+			if (it->msdu_id < DP_TX_IDR_SIZE - 1) {
+				prefetchw(&tx_ring->bufs[it->msdu_id]);
+				if (it->msdu_id < tx_ring->ext_ids)
+					prefetchw(&tx_ring->ext_map[it->msdu_id]);
+			}
 			it->msdu = NULL;
 			it->more = false;
 			it->seg.skb = NULL;
@@ -1685,12 +1694,17 @@ int ath11k_dp_tx_completion_handler(stru
 			struct ath11k_dp_tx_compl_item *it = &items[k];
 
 			/* the next frames' buffers and shared infos are cold:
-			 * the id table held only their pointers
+			 * the id table held only their pointers. The shared
+			 * info's address is in the buffer's third and fourth
+			 * line, read for k + 1 below.
 			 */
 			if (k + 2 < n && items[k + 2].msdu) {
-				prefetch(items[k + 2].msdu);
-				prefetch((u8 *)items[k + 2].msdu +
-					 L1_CACHE_BYTES);
+				u8 *p = (u8 *)items[k + 2].msdu;
+
+				prefetch(p);
+				prefetch(p + L1_CACHE_BYTES);
+				prefetch(p + 2 * L1_CACHE_BYTES);
+				prefetch(p + 3 * L1_CACHE_BYTES);
 			}
 			if (k + 1 < n && items[k + 1].msdu)
 				prefetch(skb_shinfo(items[k + 1].msdu));
